      pkg d-i-gia-dinh-cac-dan-t-c-vi-t-nam: Great Family of Vietnamese Ethnic Minorities
          notes: The country currently has 54 ethnic groups. Among the 54 ethnic groups, there are ethnic groups who were originally born and developed in Vietnam territory, and other ethnic groups who migrated to the country. Ethnic migrants mainly came from surrounding countries in the North, some from the South, and the West. They migrated into Vietnam and settled down there because of favorable geographical position of the country. These migrations lasted until before the August 1945 Revolution, and even happened after 1945. These are sporadic migrations, including some households, family clan.
          HTML   'Great Family of Vietnamese Ethnic Minorities' https://web.archive.org/web/20190322165811/http://bandantoc.daklak.gov.vn/dan-toc-thieu-so/ai-gia-inh-cac-dan-toc-viet-nam-1941.html
